{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to help users modify files by generating tool calls and complete file content.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\n**IMPORTANT**: You do NOT directly edit files. You generate tool calls that the system executes.\n\n## CORRECT WORKFLOW (CRITICAL):\n\n1. **Read the file first**: Generate a read_file tool call to get the current file content\n2. **Reason about changes**: Look at the file content (from tool response) and understand what needs to change\n3. **Generate COMPLETE file content**: Create the entire new file content as text (NOT a diff or patch)\n4. **Write the complete file**: Generate a write_file tool call with the complete new file content\n\nThe system will execute your tool calls. You never touch the filesystem directly.\n\n## CRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n\n- **ALWAYS generate the COMPLETE file content** in write_file, not just the changes\n- **NEVER generate diffs, patches, or partial content** - always the full file\n- **CRITICAL: When you read a file, use EXACTLY the content from read_file tool response**\n- **CRITICAL: When replacing text, change ONLY what the user specified - preserve everything else EXACTLY**\n- **CRITICAL: Do NOT add, remove, or modify any content that the user didn't explicitly request**\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- Do NOT add lines like \"done: true\" or \"more: false\" unless they were in the original file\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- If the user says \"add the content 'X'\", add ONLY 'X' - nothing else\n- If the file is EMPTY and user says \"add content 'X'\", the file should contain ONLY 'X' (no other content)\n- Do NOT add example content like \"line1: first line\" or \"existing content\" unless it is already in the file\n- Content to add/remove is usually specified in single or double quotes: 'text' or \"text\"\n- Extract the exact content from quotes - do not modify or interpret it\n- When reading a file, use ONLY the content that is actually in the file (from read_file tool response)\n- Do NOT infer or add content that wasn't in the file you read\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was (if any exists)\n- Follow the user instructions precisely and literally\n- Generate tool calls (read_file, write_file) that the system will execute\n- You never directly access or modify files - only generate tool calls and content"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Modify the file at `sample.txt`.\n\nRemove the line that contains 'Second' and comes after 'Section 2'\n\nRemember: Only change what is specified. Preserve all other content exactly as it is in the file."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I will read the file to see its current content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"sample.txt\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "Section 1: First section\nLine with 'Second' in it\nSection 2: Second section\nAnother line with 'Second' word\nSection 3: Third section", "tool_call_id": "call_e075e9aa1017"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I have read the file. Now I will make only the requested change and generate the complete updated file content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"sample.txt\", \"contents\": \"Section 1: First section\\nLine with 'Second' in it\\nSection 2: Second section\\nSection 3: Third section\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_fff218ca19b5"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. I have made only the requested change and preserved all other content."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to help users modify files by generating tool calls and complete file content.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\n**IMPORTANT**: You do NOT directly edit files. You generate tool calls that the system executes.\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Generate tool calls (read_file, write_file) that the system will execute\n- You never directly access or modify files - only generate tool calls and content\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create default/example content unless the user explicitly requests it\n- If the user says \"create a file X\" without specifying content, create an EMPTY file\n- Do NOT add \"test: 1\" or any default content to YAML files\n- Do NOT add default structure to JSON files\n- Only create the exact content the user describes\n- If no content is specified, use write_file with empty contents\n- Follow the user instructions precisely"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Create a new file at `sample.txt`"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I will create the new file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"sample.txt\", \"contents\": \"\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_8a4503c832b0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. The file has been created."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to help users modify files by generating tool calls and complete file content.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\n**IMPORTANT**: You do NOT directly edit files. You generate tool calls that the system executes.\n\n## CORRECT WORKFLOW (CRITICAL):\n\n1. **Read the file first**: Generate a read_file tool call to get the current file content\n2. **Reason about changes**: Look at the file content (from tool response) and understand what needs to change\n3. **Generate COMPLETE file content**: Create the entire new file content as text (NOT a diff or patch)\n4. **Write the complete file**: Generate a write_file tool call with the complete new file content\n\nThe system will execute your tool calls. You never touch the filesystem directly.\n\n## CRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n\n- **ALWAYS generate the COMPLETE file content** in write_file, not just the changes\n- **NEVER generate diffs, patches, or partial content** - always the full file\n- **CRITICAL: When you read a file, use EXACTLY the content from read_file tool response**\n- **CRITICAL: When replacing text, change ONLY what the user specified - preserve everything else EXACTLY**\n- **CRITICAL: Do NOT add, remove, or modify any content that the user didn't explicitly request**\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- Do NOT add lines like \"done: true\" or \"more: false\" unless they were in the original file\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- If the user says \"add the content 'X'\", add ONLY 'X' - nothing else\n- If the file is EMPTY and user says \"add content 'X'\", the file should contain ONLY 'X' (no other content)\n- Do NOT add example content like \"line1: first line\" or \"existing content\" unless it is already in the file\n- Content to add/remove is usually specified in single or double quotes: 'text' or \"text\"\n- Extract the exact content from quotes - do not modify or interpret it\n- When reading a file, use ONLY the content that is actually in the file (from read_file tool response)\n- Do NOT infer or add content that wasn't in the file you read\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was (if any exists)\n- Follow the user instructions precisely and literally\n- Generate tool calls (read_file, write_file) that the system will execute\n- You never directly access or modify files - only generate tool calls and content"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Modify the file at `config.py`.\n\nAdd a discount parameter (default 0.0) to calculate_total and apply it to the total before returning\n\nRemember: Only change what is specified. Preserve all other content exactly as it is in the file."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I will read the file to see its current content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"config.py\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "def calculate_total(items):\n    total = 0\n    for item in items:\n        total += item['price']\n    return total\n", "tool_call_id": "call_edb8e737340f"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I have read the file. Now I will make only the requested change and generate the complete updated file content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"config.py\", \"contents\": \"def calculate_total(items, discount=0.0):\\n    total = 0\\n    for item in items:\\n        total += item['price']\\n    total = total * (1 - discount)\\n    return total\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_4f6dbcce6c0b"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. I have made only the requested change and preserved all other content."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to help users modify files by generating tool calls and complete file content.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\n**IMPORTANT**: You do NOT directly edit files. You generate tool calls that the system executes.\n\n## CORRECT WORKFLOW (CRITICAL):\n\n1. **Read the file first**: Generate a read_file tool call to get the current file content\n2. **Reason about changes**: Look at the file content (from tool response) and understand what needs to change\n3. **Generate COMPLETE file content**: Create the entire new file content as text (NOT a diff or patch)\n4. **Write the complete file**: Generate a write_file tool call with the complete new file content\n\nThe system will execute your tool calls. You never touch the filesystem directly.\n\n## CRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n\n- **ALWAYS generate the COMPLETE file content** in write_file, not just the changes\n- **NEVER generate diffs, patches, or partial content** - always the full file\n- **CRITICAL: When you read a file, use EXACTLY the content from read_file tool response**\n- **CRITICAL: When replacing text, change ONLY what the user specified - preserve everything else EXACTLY**\n- **CRITICAL: Do NOT add, remove, or modify any content that the user didn't explicitly request**\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- Do NOT add lines like \"done: true\" or \"more: false\" unless they were in the original file\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- If the user says \"add the content 'X'\", add ONLY 'X' - nothing else\n- If the file is EMPTY and user says \"add content 'X'\", the file should contain ONLY 'X' (no other content)\n- Do NOT add example content like \"line1: first line\" or \"existing content\" unless it is already in the file\n- Content to add/remove is usually specified in single or double quotes: 'text' or \"text\"\n- Extract the exact content from quotes - do not modify or interpret it\n- When reading a file, use ONLY the content that is actually in the file (from read_file tool response)\n- Do NOT infer or add content that wasn't in the file you read\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was (if any exists)\n- Follow the user instructions precisely and literally\n- Generate tool calls (read_file, write_file) that the system will execute\n- You never directly access or modify files - only generate tool calls and content"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Modify the file at `docs.md`.\n\nUpdate the code block: add a name parameter with default 'World' and use an f-string in the print statement\n\nRemember: Only change what is specified. Preserve all other content exactly as it is in the file."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I will read the file to see its current content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"docs.md\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "# Example\n\nHere is some code:\n\n```python\ndef hello():\n    print(\"Hello\")\n```\n", "tool_call_id": "call_38f756275a7a"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I have read the file. Now I will make only the requested change and generate the complete updated file content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"docs.md\", \"contents\": \"# Example\\n\\nHere is some code:\\n\\n```python\\ndef hello(name=\\\"World\\\"):\\n    print(f\\\"Hello, {name}\\\")\\n```\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_d6fd85335377"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. I have made only the requested change and preserved all other content."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to help users modify files by generating tool calls and complete file content.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\n**IMPORTANT**: You do NOT directly edit files. You generate tool calls that the system executes.\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Generate tool calls (read_file, write_file) that the system will execute\n- You never directly access or modify files - only generate tool calls and content\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create default/example content unless the user explicitly requests it\n- If the user says \"create a file X\" without specifying content, create an EMPTY file\n- Do NOT add \"test: 1\" or any default content to YAML files\n- Do NOT add default structure to JSON files\n- Only create the exact content the user describes\n- If no content is specified, use write_file with empty contents: \"\"\n- Follow the user instructions precisely"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Create a new Python file at `script.py` with a main function that prints 'Hello, World!'"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I will create the new file with the requested structure."}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_cabf00175766"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. The file has been created."}]}
