 says \"add content 'X'\", the file should contain ONLY 'X' (no other content)\n- Do NOT add example content like \"line1: first line\" or \"existing content\" unless it is already in the file\n- Content to add/remove is usually specified in single or double quotes: 'text' or \"text\"\n- Extract the exact content from quotes - do not modify or interpret it\n- When reading a file, use ONLY the content that is actually in the file (from read_file tool response)\n- Do NOT infer or add content that wasn't in the file you read\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was (if any exists)\n- Follow the user instructions precisely and literally\n- Generate tool calls (read_file, write_file) that the system will execute\n- You never directly access or modify files - only generate tool calls and content"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Modify the file at `data.json`.\n\nReplace the paragraph starting with 'Foo' with: 'This is the new paragraph content.'\n\nRemember: Only change what is specified. Preserve all other content exactly as it is in the file."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I will read the file to see its current content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"data.json\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "Introduction paragraph\nThis is a long paragraph starting with 'Foo' that contains\nmultiple lines of text that need to be replaced.\nThe paragraph continues here.\nEnd of paragraph\nConclusion paragraph", "tool_call_id": "call_2c28a78edec2"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I have read the file. Now I will make only the requested change and generate the complete updated file content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"data.json\", \"contents\": \"Introduction paragraph\\nThis is the new paragraph content.\\nConclusion paragraph\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_ed806c90c5f1"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. I have made only the requested change and preserved all other content."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to help users modify files by generating tool calls and complete file content.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only manipulate the text the user describes\n- Follow the user instructions precisely\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files\n- If the user asks to confirm or check contents without changes, only read the file"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Check the contents of `sample.txt` and confirm what is in it. Do not make any changes."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I will read the file to check its contents.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"sample.txt\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "Line 1: First line\nLine 2: Second line\nLine 3: Third line", "tool_call_id": "call_a72bcf9b4262"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "The file `sample.txt` contains:\n\nLine 1: First line\nLine 2: Second line\nLine 3: Third line\n\nNo changes were made as requested."}]}
