{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to help users modify files by generating tool calls and complete file content.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\n**IMPORTANT**: You do NOT directly edit files. You generate tool calls that the system executes.\n\n## CORRECT WORKFLOW (CRITICAL):\n\n1. **Read the file first**: Generate a read_file tool call to get the current file content\n2. **Reason about changes**: Look at the file content (from tool response) and understand what needs to change\n3. **Generate COMPLETE file content**: Create the entire new file content as text (NOT a diff or patch)\n4. **Write the complete file**: Generate a write_file tool call with the complete new file content\n\nThe system will execute your tool calls. You never touch the filesystem directly.\n\n## CRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n\n- **ALWAYS generate the COMPLETE file content** in write_file, not just the changes\n- **NEVER generate diffs, patches, or partial content** - always the full file\n- **CRITICAL: When you read a file, use EXACTLY the content from read_file tool response**\n- **CRITICAL: When replacing text, change ONLY what the user specified - preserve everything else EXACTLY**\n- **CRITICAL: Do NOT add, remove, or modify any content that the user didn't explicitly request**\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- Do NOT add lines like \"done: true\" or \"more: false\" unless they were in the original file\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- If the user says \"add the content 'X'\", add ONLY 'X' - nothing else\n- If the file is EMPTY and user says \"add content 'X'\", the file should contain ONLY 'X' (no other content)\n- Do NOT add example content like \"line1: first line\" or \"existing content\" unless it is already in the file\n- Content to add/remove is usually specified in single or double quotes: 'text' or \"text\"\n- Extract the exact content from quotes - do not modify or interpret it\n- When reading a file, use ONLY the content that is actually in the file (from read_file tool response)\n- Do NOT infer or add content that wasn't in the file you read\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was (if any exists)\n- Follow the user instructions precisely and literally\n- Generate tool calls (read_file, write_file) that the system will execute\n- You never directly access or modify files - only generate tool calls and content"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Modify the file at `data.json`.\n\nAdd the content 'hey: 1' to the file\n\nRemember: Only change what is specified. Preserve all other content exactly as it is in the file."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I will read the file to see its current content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"data.json\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "", "tool_call_id": "call_e5204f63c3a6"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I have read the file. Now I will make only the requested change and generate the complete updated file content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"data.json\", \"contents\": \"hey: 1\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_d710b1702586"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. I have made only the requested change and preserved all other content."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to help users modify files by generating tool calls and complete file content.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\n**IMPORTANT**: You do NOT directly edit files. You generate tool calls that the system executes.\n\n## CORRECT WORKFLOW (CRITICAL):\n\n1. **Read the file first**: Generate a read_file tool call to get the current file content\n2. **Reason about changes**: Look at the file content (from tool response) and understand what needs to change\n3. **Generate COMPLETE file content**: Create the entire new file content as text (NOT a diff or patch)\n4. **Write the complete file**: Generate a write_file tool call with the complete new file content\n\nThe system will execute your tool calls. You never touch the filesystem directly.\n\n## CRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n\n- **ALWAYS generate the COMPLETE file content** in write_file, not just the changes\n- **NEVER generate diffs, patches, or partial content** - always the full file\n- **CRITICAL: When you read a file, use EXACTLY the content from read_file tool response**\n- **CRITICAL: When replacing text, change ONLY what the user specified - preserve everything else EXACTLY**\n- **CRITICAL: Do NOT add, remove, or modify any content that the user didn't explicitly request**\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- Do NOT add lines like \"done: true\" or \"more: false\" unless they were in the original file\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- If the user says \"add the content 'X'\", add ONLY 'X' - nothing else\n- If the file is EMPTY and user says \"add content 'X'\", the file should contain ONLY 'X' (no other content)\n- Do NOT add example content like \"line1: first line\" or \"existing content\" unless it is already in the file\n- Content to add/remove is usually specified in single or double quotes: 'text' or \"text\"\n- Extract the exact content from quotes - do not modify or interpret it\n- When reading a file, use ONLY the content that is actually in the file (from read_file tool response)\n- Do NOT infer or add content that wasn't in the file you read\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was (if any exists)\n- Follow the user instructions precisely and literally\n- Generate tool calls (read_file, write_file) that the system will execute\n- You never directly access or modify files - only generate tool calls and content"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Modify the file at `example.txt`.\n\nReplace lines 3-4 with:\nLine 3: Updated third line\nLine 4: Updated fourth line\n\nRemember: Only change what is specified. Preserve all other content exactly as it is in the file."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I will read the file to see its current content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"example.txt\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "Line 1: First line\nLine 2: Second line\nLine 3: Third line\nLine 4: Fourth line\nLine 5: Fifth line", "tool_call_id": "call_c25d923c7c79"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I have read the file. Now I will make only the requested change and generate the complete updated file content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"example.txt\", \"contents\": \"Line 1: First line\\nLine 2: Second line\\nLine 3: Updated third line\\nLine 4: Updated fourth line\\nLine 5: Fifth line\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_962ae254c254"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. I have made only the requested change and preserved all other content."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to help users modify files by generating tool calls and complete file content.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\n**IMPORTANT**: You do NOT directly edit files. You generate tool calls that the system executes.\n\n## CORRECT WORKFLOW (CRITICAL):\n\n1. **Read the file first**: Generate a read_file tool call to get the current file content\n2. **Reason about changes**: Look at the file content (from tool response) and understand what needs to change\n3. **Generate COMPLETE file content**: Create the entire new file content as text (NOT a diff or patch)\n4. **Write the complete file**: Generate a write_file tool call with the complete new file content\n\nThe system will execute your tool calls. You never touch the filesystem directly.\n\n## CRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n\n- **ALWAYS generate the COMPLETE file content** in write_file, not just the changes\n- **NEVER generate diffs, patches, or partial content** - always the full file\n- **CRITICAL: When you read a file, use EXACTLY the content from read_file tool response**\n- **CRITICAL: When replacing text, change ONLY what the user specified - preserve everything else EXACTLY**\n- **CRITICAL: Do NOT add, remove, or modify any content that the user didn't explicitly request**\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- Do NOT add lines like \"done: true\" or \"more: false\" unless they were in the original file\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- If the user says \"add the content 'X'\", add ONLY 'X' - nothing else\n- If the file is EMPTY and user says \"add content 'X'\", the file should contain ONLY 'X' (no other content)\n- Do NOT add example content like \"line1: first line\" or \"existing content\" unless it is already in the file\n- Content to add/remove is usually specified in single or double quotes: 'text' or \"text\"\n- Extract the exact content from quotes - do not modify or interpret it\n- When reading a file, use ONLY the content that is actually in the file (from read_file tool response)\n- Do NOT infer or add content that wasn't in the file you read\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was (if any exists)\n- Follow the user instructions precisely and literally\n- Generate tool calls (read_file, write_file) that the system will execute\n- You never directly access or modify files - only generate tool calls and content"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Modify the file at `example.txt`.\n\nAdd the content 'hey: 1' to the file\n\nRemember: Only change what is specified. Preserve all other content exactly as it is in the file."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I will read the file to see its current content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"example.txt\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "existing content\nmore content", "tool_call_id": "call_1ae0b5ca69b9"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I have read the file. Now I will make only the requested change and generate the complete updated file content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"example.txt\", \"contents\": \"existing content\\nmore content\\nhey: 1\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_644b07ce0a80"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. I have made only the requested change and preserved all other content."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to help users modify files by generating tool calls and complete file content.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\n**IMPORTANT**: You do NOT directly edit files. You generate tool calls that the system executes.\n\n## CORRECT WORKFLOW (CRITICAL):\n\n1. **Read the file first**: Generate a read_file tool call to get the current file content\n2. **Reason about changes**: Look at the file content (from tool response) and understand what needs to change\n3. **Generate COMPLETE file content**: Create the entire new file content as text (NOT a diff or patch)\n4. **Write the complete file**: Generate a write_file tool call with the complete new file content\n\nThe system will execute your tool calls. You never touch the filesystem directly.\n\n## CRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n\n- **ALWAYS generate the COMPLETE file content** in write_file, not just the changes\n- **NEVER generate diffs, patches, or partial content** - always the full file\n- **CRITICAL: When you read a file, use EXACTLY the content from read_file tool response**\n- **CRITICAL: When replacing text, change ONLY what the user specified - preserve everything else EXACTLY**\n- **CRITICAL: Do NOT add, remove, or modify any content that the user didn't explicitly request**\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- Do NOT add lines like \"done: true\" or \"more: false\" unless they were in the original file\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- If the user says \"add the content 'X'\", add ONLY 'X' - nothing else\n- If the file is EMPTY and user says \"add content 'X'\", the file should contain ONLY 'X' (no other content)\n- Do NOT add example content like \"line1: first line\" or \"existing content\" unless it is already in the file\n- Content to add/remove is usually specified in single or double quotes: 'text' or \"text\"\n- Extract the exact content from quotes - do not modify or interpret it\n- When reading a file, use ONLY the content that is actually in the file (from read_file tool response)\n- Do NOT infer or add content that wasn't in the file you read\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was (if any exists)\n- Follow the user instructions precisely and literally\n- Generate tool calls (read_file, write_file) that the system will execute\n- You never directly access or modify files - only generate tool calls and content"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Modify the file at `input.txt`.\n\nReplace the word 'stuff' with 'blah'\n\nRemember: Only change what is specified. Preserve all other content exactly as it is in the file."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I will read the file to see its current content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"input.txt\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "package main\n\nimport \"fmt\"\n\nfunc main() {\n    fmt.Println(\"Hello, stuff.\")\n    fmt.Println(\"This is a test.\")\n    fmt.Println(\"Another line.\")\n}", "tool_call_id": "call_073d495cfd38"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I have read the file. Now I will make only the requested change and generate the complete updated file content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"input.txt\", \"contents\": \"package main\\n\\nimport \\\"fmt\\\"\\n\\nfunc main() {\\n    fmt.Println(\\\"Hello, blah.\\\")\\n    fmt.Println(\\\"This is a test.\\\")\\n    fmt.Println(\\\"Another line.\\\")\\n}\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_67e8fdda7327"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. I have made only the requested change and preserved all other content."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to help users modify files by generating tool calls and complete file content.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\n**IMPORTANT**: You do NOT directly edit files. You generate tool calls that the system executes.\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Generate tool calls (read_file, write_file) that the system will execute\n- You never directly access or modify files - only generate tool calls and content\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create default/example content unless the user explicitly requests it\n- If the user says \"create a file X\" without specifying content, create an EMPTY file\n- Do NOT add \"test: 1\" or any default content to YAML files\n- Do NOT add default structure to JSON files\n- Only create the exact content the user describes\n- If no content is specified, use write_file with empty contents\n- Follow the user instructions precisely"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Create a new file at `file.txt`"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I will create the new file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"file.txt\", \"contents\": \"\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_637ec4da6e10"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. The file has been created."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to help users modify files by generating tool calls and complete file content.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\n**IMPORTANT**: You do NOT directly edit files. You generate tool calls that the system executes.\n\n## CORRECT WORKFLOW (CRITICAL):\n\n1. **Read the file first**: Generate a read_file tool call to get the current file content\n2. **Reason about changes**: Look at the file content (from tool response) and understand what needs to change\n3. **Generate COMPLETE file content**: Create the entire new file content as text (NOT a diff or patch)\n4. **Write the complete file**: Generate a write_file tool call with the complete new file content\n\nThe system will execute your tool calls. You never touch the filesystem directly.\n\n## CRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n\n- **ALWAYS generate the COMPLETE file content** in write_file, not just the changes\n- **NEVER generate diffs, patches, or partial content** - always the full file\n- **CRITICAL: When you read a file, use EXACTLY the content from read_file tool response**\n- **CRITICAL: When replacing text, change ONLY what the user specified - preserve everything else EXACTLY**\n- **CRITICAL: Do NOT add, remove, or modify any content that the user didn't explicitly request**\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- Do NOT add lines like \"done: true\" or \"more: false\" unless they were in the original file\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- If the user says \"add the content 'X'\", add ONLY 'X' - nothing else\n- If the file is EMPTY and user says \"add content 'X'\", the file should contain ONLY 'X' (no other content)\n- Do NOT add example content like \"line1: first line\" or \"existing content\" unless it is already in the file\n- Content to add/remove is usually specified in single or double quotes: 'text' or \"text\"\n- Extract the exact content from quotes - do not modify or interpret it\n- When reading a file, use ONLY the content that is actually in the file (from read_file tool response)\n- Do NOT infer or add content that wasn't in the file you read\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was (if any exists)\n- Follow the user instructions precisely and literally\n- Generate tool calls (read_file, write_file) that the system will execute\n- You never directly access or modify files - only generate tool calls and content"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Modify the file at `k8s.yaml`.\n\nSet cache to true, add analytics: true under features, and set debug to false\n\nRemember: Only change what is specified. Preserve all other content exactly as it is in the file."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I will read the file to see its current content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"k8s.yaml\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "app:\n  features:\n    auth: true\n    cache: false\n  settings:\n    debug: true\n", "tool_call_id": "call_d28c9d0598c3"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I have read the file. Now I will make only the requested change and generate the complete updated file content.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"k8s.yaml\", \"contents\": \"app:\\n  features:\\n    auth: true\\n    cache: true\\n    analytics: true\\n  settings:\\n    debug: false\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_b78bdf04b579"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. I have made only the requested change and preserved all other content."}]}
